# MANDATORY: Google Calendar (Voice V3 provider)

Read **both** before any Google Calendar work:

1. **`docs/GOOGLE-CALENDAR-INTEGRATION-ENGINEERING-GUIDE.md`** — Google Calendar API v3, OAuth, `calendar.events.owned`, events CRUD, normalization, errors.
2. **`docs/GOOGLE-CALENDAR-VOICE-V3-IMPLEMENTATION-DIRECTIVE.md`** — end-to-end wiring, UI, wizard, compile/runtime, definition of done.
3. **`docs/GOOGLE-CALENDAR-DATETIME-PROVIDER-BOUNDARY.md`** — **date/time provider boundary** (canonical Transovo time → Google serializer/normalizer; Microsoft frozen).

OAuth scope review template: **`docs/GOOGLE-CALENDAR-OAUTH-VERIFICATION.md`**

## When this rule activates

Implementing, changing, debugging, or reviewing Google Calendar OAuth, Integrations UI, Appointment Receptionist wizard scheduling provider, Voice V3 scheduling executors, or Google provider adapter code.

## Architecture (locked)

- **ADD GOOGLE. DO NOT REBUILD SCHEDULING.**
- Google is a **provider behind existing tools** — `find_availability`, `book_appointment`, `find_appointment`, `reschedule_appointment`, `cancel_appointment`.
- **Do NOT** add `google_*` FunctionTools or Google-specific Astra tools if Microsoft does not work that way.
- **Astra does NOT choose Microsoft vs Google** — published wizard config selects provider; Astra calls the same Transovo scheduling tools.
- **Microsoft 365 is FROZEN** — trace as read-only behavioral reference; copy contracts/patterns; **do not refactor Microsoft** while adding Google. Microsoft tests must stay green.

## Wizard / Calendly

- Replace **visible** Calendly choice in Appointment Receptionist wizard with **Google Calendar** (Microsoft · Google · Send booking link).
- **Do NOT** delete Calendly platform code (MCTB, legacy configs).

## Date/time (locked)

- Caller language is normalized **only** upstream (`scheduling-normalizer` / `set_scheduling_preference`).
- Google code consumes **canonical UTC instants + IANA business timezone** from the scheduling engine.
- Use `google-datetime-adapter.ts` for writes; `google-event-interval-normalizer.ts` for reads.
- **Never** pass Microsoft Graph payloads or raw `...Z` strings as Google `dateTime` when `timeZone` is IANA.
- Availability reads must handle **timed and all-day** Google events (exclusive all-day `end.date`).

## API / OAuth (summary — full detail in engineering guide)

- Scope: `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events.owned` only for V1.
- Calendar: `primary`; availability via paginated `events.list` (not FreeBusy for V1).
- Reschedule: **GET + UPDATE**, not default PATCH.
- Extend existing Google OAuth; offline refresh; never overwrite stored refresh token with null.

## Prohibited without explicit approval

Broad `calendar` scope, new scheduling framework, Google logic in Amy/Astra prompts, LLM appointment matching, refactoring Microsoft executors, MCTB pipeline changes, purging Calendly from repo.

## On conflict

Official Google docs → client types → existing Transovo provider architecture → engineering guide → implementation directive.
